WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.787 --> 00:00:03.726
♫ In my dreams

00:00:03.726 --> 00:00:06.559
♫ I see your face

00:00:07.526 --> 00:00:10.076
♫ Walk with you

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.743
♫ Hold you safe

00:00:14.338 --> 00:00:17.445
- [Father] My son Lee,
he went missing in 1988,

00:00:17.445 --> 00:00:19.181
on September the 10th.

00:00:19.181 --> 00:00:21.091
- [Father] My daughter
Claudia went missing eight

00:00:21.091 --> 00:00:24.514
and a half years ago, when she was 35.

00:00:24.514 --> 00:00:26.402
- My brother's a missing person.

00:00:26.402 --> 00:00:28.558
He's been missing for 22 years.

00:00:28.558 --> 00:00:30.774
And that's why I joined the choir to meet

00:00:30.774 --> 00:00:35.251
other families and have
support from the choir.

00:00:35.251 --> 00:00:37.250
- The Missing People Choir is made up

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.006
of family's with missing loved ones

00:00:39.006 --> 00:00:42.138
and volunteers that want to sing with us.

00:00:42.138 --> 00:00:44.888
- I sing my heart out for my boy.

00:00:46.882 --> 00:00:48.549
I can't talk to him,

00:00:50.389 --> 00:00:53.984
but I sing, I sing to him all the time

00:00:53.984 --> 00:00:55.984
when I'm with the choir.

00:00:56.952 --> 00:00:58.256
- Connecting with other people

00:00:58.256 --> 00:01:02.523
who've had a missing loved
one is really special.

00:01:02.523 --> 00:01:06.001
And for me, it was 19
years before I met anybody

00:01:06.001 --> 00:01:07.833
who was in the same situation.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.457
You know, we know what each of us has gone through

00:01:10.457 --> 00:01:12.968
and we just connect with each other

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:15.624
in a very particular way.

00:01:15.624 --> 00:01:17.874
(laughing)

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.763
- [James] Britain's Got
Talent was an incredible,

00:01:22.763 --> 00:01:24.766
a juggernaut of an experience.

00:01:24.766 --> 00:01:27.099
♫ Touch you

00:01:28.172 --> 00:01:29.005
- That's incredible.

00:01:29.005 --> 00:01:31.976
(cheering and applause)

00:01:31.976 --> 00:01:34.495
- [James] Our win wasn't going
to be the big prize money

00:01:34.495 --> 00:01:36.344
or a big single or anything like that,

00:01:36.344 --> 00:01:38.552
it was actually, find someone.

00:01:38.552 --> 00:01:40.633
That's what we went out to achieve.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.816
- One young man even came back

00:01:42.816 --> 00:01:45.504
because he saw his face on the appeals,

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.231
and he'd been missing for six weeks.

00:01:47.231 --> 00:01:48.197
He was only a young boy

00:01:48.197 --> 00:01:50.081
and he reconnected with his mother

00:01:50.081 --> 00:01:53.164
after listening to us singing on BGT.

00:01:54.919 --> 00:01:57.919
- Where words end, music carries on.

00:01:59.569 --> 00:02:03.728
And so when you apply it to
causes that really matter

00:02:03.728 --> 00:02:05.494
and that resonate with people,

00:02:05.494 --> 00:02:08.274
you know, it's extremely powerful stuff.

00:02:08.274 --> 00:02:10.073
And it's beautiful.

00:02:10.073 --> 00:02:10.906
- Daughter.

00:02:10.906 --> 00:02:11.739
- Son.

00:02:11.739 --> 00:02:12.572
- Brother.

00:02:12.572 --> 00:02:13.420
- Son.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.253
- Son.

00:02:15.228 --> 00:02:17.645
♫ I miss you

